      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-3\\left(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-3\\left(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-3\\left(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)+{e}^{y}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(-3\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-3\\left(+{e}^{y}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{j}+(-3\\left(+\\frac{1}{z}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,y={t}^{2},$ and $z=\\frac{1}{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(-3\\left(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-3\\left(+{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{j}+(-3\\left(+t\\right))\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\mathbf{i}+2t\\,\\mathbf{j}-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((-3\\left(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-3\\left(+{e}^{{t}^{2}}\\right))\\,\\mathbf{j}+(-3\\left(+t\\right))\\,\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\mathbf{i}+2t\\,\\mathbf{j}-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\mathbf{k}) \\\\  & =-3\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{t}{{t}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =-3\\left(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
