    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dedf0d65-e848-5cd8-a829-bee9c91c19d6",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x,y,z)=-1\\left(x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\right)$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+((t + 2)+1)\\,\\mathbf{j}+((t + 2)-1)\\,\\mathbf{k},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "144bbef3-5c18-51d5-8b4f-f8278b001466",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "ff4fbe71-da1c-5699-ba1b-e7a76648b34a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "- 2 \\left(t \\ln{\\left(t + 2 \\right)} + \\frac{2 t}{t + 2} + 3 \\ln{\\left(t + 2 \\right)} + \\frac{4}{t + 2}\\right)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "88333c73-3975-5f03-a174-9f153e9042a5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "- 4 \\ln{\\left(t + 2 \\right)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "118d2770-1ede-56ea-8b09-08110ac765fa",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "- 12 \\left(t + 2\\right) \\ln{\\left(t + 2 \\right)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e836f0be-0794-5f78-9a03-912be8fd9267",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "2 \\left(t \\ln{\\left(t + 2 \\right)} - \\frac{2 t}{t + 2} + \\ln{\\left(t + 2 \\right)} - \\frac{4}{t + 2}\\right)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "4928e0e5-2c7d-57fe-87b0-4349701eb333",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-1\\left(4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)+1)\\right)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "4928e0e5-2c7d-57fe-87b0-4349701eb333"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}[-1\\left(x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\right)]\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}[-1\\left(x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\right)]\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{∂}{∂z}[-1\\left(x({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\right)]\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(-1\\left(({y}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\right))\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-1\\left(+2xy\\right))\\,\\mathbf{j}+(-1\\left(-2xz\\right))\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2),$ $y=(t + 2)+1$ and $z=(t + 2)-1$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(-1\\left([((t + 2)+1)^{2}-((t + 2)-1)^{2}]\\right))\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-1\\left(+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\cdot ((t + 2)+1)\\right))\\,\\mathbf{j}+(-1\\left(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\cdot ((t + 2)-1)\\right))\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(-1\\left(4(t + 2)\\right))\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-1\\left(+2((t + 2)+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\right))\\,\\mathbf{j}+(-1\\left(-2((t + 2)-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\right))\\,\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2))\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t + 2)+1)\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t + 2)-1)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{(t + 2)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(1)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(1)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((-1\\left(4(t + 2)\\right))\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-1\\left(+2((t + 2)+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\right))\\,\\mathbf{j}+(-1\\left(-2((t + 2)-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\right))\\,\\mathbf{k})\\cdot (\\left(\\frac{1}{(t + 2)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(1)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(1)\\,\\mathbf{k}) \\\\  & =-1\\left(4(t + 2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{(t + 2)}+2((t + 2)+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\cdot 1-2((t + 2)-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\cdot 1\\right) \\\\  & =-1\\left(4+2((t + 2)+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)-2((t + 2)-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\right) \\\\  & =-1\\left(4+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)\\right) \\\\  & =-1\\left(4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t + 2)+1)\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
